ISHA — Local JARVIS-Style Autonomous Assistant

Master Development Specification for Claude

1. PROJECT GOAL

I have an existing Python desktop AI assistant project named ISHA.

The existing source file is:

"mani.py"

Do NOT treat this as a new project.

Your task is to upgrade the existing ISHA project into an advanced, local-first, JARVIS-style autonomous desktop assistant.

The goal is NOT to create an ordinary chatbot.

The goal is to create an AGI-style autonomous PC assistant that can understand natural language, reason about tasks, choose appropriate tools/models, execute multi-step operations, observe results, recover from failures, and communicate naturally with the user.

The inspiration is the fictional JARVIS concept from Iron Man/Avengers, but implementation must use realistic technologies available on the user's PC.

---

2. MOST IMPORTANT RULE

PRESERVE THE EXISTING ISHA PROJECT

Before changing anything:

1. Read the ENTIRE "mani.py".
2. Understand its architecture.
3. Identify existing classes, tools, functions, GUI components, model backend, agent loop, configuration system, memory system, TTS/STT, OS-control layer and WhatsApp implementation.
4. Do NOT rewrite the entire application blindly.
5. Do NOT remove existing working functionality just to implement new functionality.
6. Reuse existing code wherever practical.
7. Refactor only when necessary.
8. Maintain backward compatibility with existing configuration where possible.
9. If a feature already exists, improve it instead of creating a duplicate implementation.

The current source already contains significant functionality. Build on it.

