4. LOCAL-FIRST REQUIREMENT

ISHA must be local-first.

Primary AI inference should run locally using GGUF/llama.cpp or another supported local backend.

Internet must NOT be required for ordinary:

- conversation
- reasoning
- coding
- file search
- file management
- system information
- PC control
- local memory
- local model inference

Internet may be used when the user explicitly requests something that inherently requires internet access, such as:

- downloading software
- opening websites
- web search
- downloading a model
- downloading a dependency
- WhatsApp Web communication
- online services

Clearly separate:

LOCAL AI
from
ONLINE ACTIONS

The AI brain should remain local.

