25. PERMISSION SYSTEM

Maintain a strict risk model.

Suggested tiers:

SAFE
CONFIRM
CRITICAL

SAFE

Examples:

- read file
- search files
- check RAM
- check storage
- screenshot
- open calculator
- open browser

CONFIRM

Examples:

- delete file
- uninstall software
- empty trash
- modify important settings
- send message
- overwrite files

CRITICAL

Examples:

- arbitrary shell commands
- system-wide modifications
- privileged operations
- destructive recursive operations

New tools should default to:

CONFIRM

until explicitly classified.

The existing "execute_tool()" validation and risk-tier architecture should be preserved.

